NAME
       fcntl - manipulate a file descriptor

SYNOPSIS
       #include <fcntl.h>

       int fcntl(int fd, int cmd, ... );

DESCRIPTION
       Operates on the descriptor itself rather than on the file.

COMMANDS
       F_DUPFD   duplicate FD to the lowest number at or above the
                 third argument
       F_GETFD, F_SETFD   read or set the close-on-exec flag
       F_GETFL, F_SETFL   read or set the status flags

NOTES
       Putting a terminal into non-blocking mode is done with the
       TIOCSNONBLOCK ioctl, not with F_SETFL. See ioctl(2).

RETURN VALUE
       Depends on the command, -1 with errno set on failure.

ERRORS
       EBADF    fd is not open
       EINVAL   the command is not supported

SEE ALSO
       ioctl(2), open(2), dup(2)
